# MSS-043: Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Goal: keep Linux image layers hermetic and small. In particular the default
# Compose mode must never inherit host node_modules, build output, local
# SQLite files or the read-only control checkout. Every COPY source in the
# Dockerfile must still exist with exact case; scripts/check-casing.py guards
# that, so do not add exclusions for files the image build needs.

.git
control/

# Frontend: container installs/builds its own deterministic dependencies.
**/node_modules
**/dist

# .NET build artifacts (the image restores/publishes from source).
**/bin
**/obj
**/TestResults

# Locally built frontend copied into the ASP.NET host: the web-build stage
# regenerates this from source, so host output must not enter the context.
src/MtgSoloSports/wwwroot

# Runtime data: per-save SQLite files, catalog DB, WAL/SHM sidecars.
# User data lives in the named Compose volume, never in the image.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
/data/
/saves/
/catalog/

# IDE / OS noise.
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
